@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor #6b7280
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #fdfdfd
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af

title Internal callback  —  incoming-call type 5\nA finished satellite tool calls back; the navigator verifies our own signature, closes the render-ledger entry, and folds the document into the page

participant "satellite tool\n(FindCare, e.g. provider_detail)" as TOOL
participant "UniversalNavigatorProxy\n(satellite)" as PXY
participant "Gate (facade)\n(SharedServices transport)" as GATE
participant "UniversalNavigator\n(SharedServices)" as UN
database "render ledger + sessions\n(repo rows)" as REPO
participant "Client stream\n(the waiting person)" as CLIENT

note over UN, REPO
  Earlier this turn the navigator SIGNED the page's dispatch out
  (our_signature) and recorded each required_member as a
  render-ledger expectation. A completeness budget is now racing
  the callbacks.
end note

== the satellite finishes and calls back ==
TOOL -> TOOL : work complete (recursion-guarded)
TOOL --> PXY : return document
PXY -> GATE : POST across the wire\nroute tool_completion, our_signature attached
note right of GATE
  The gate is dumb transport: it collects
  the head and params and hands them on.
  It verifies nothing and owns no route.
end note
GATE -> UN : pass(head, params, signature)

== triage — which of the five call types? ==
UN -> UN : route is known in the map;\ncall_type = internal_callback;\ndeclared proof = our_signature

alt signature verifies (SHARED-SIGNING-KEY)
  UN -> REPO : ledger: close this required_member's entry
  UN -> UN : serial deterministic merge (shared-lib fold)
  break page-merge conflict   (on_conflict = raise)
    UN -> REPO : instrument conflict\n(timings, severity = impact)
    UN -> UN : RAISE ChatHealthyException
  end
  UN -> REPO : reconcile page vs required_members
  alt every required_member closed within budget
    UN -> GATE : stream the reconciled page
    GATE -> CLIENT : event: page rendered
  else render budget expired first
    UN -> REPO : instrument timeout\n(timings, severity = impact)
    UN -> GATE : respond anyway — layman on_timeout explanation
    GATE -> CLIENT : event: partial page + explanation
  end
else bad or absent signature
  UN -> REPO : instrument bad-signature\n(timings, severity = impact)
  UN -> UN : RAISE ChatHealthyException
end

== or the required callback never arrives ==
REPO -> UN : callback_timeout wins the race\n(the required member never closed)
UN -> REPO : instrument missing-required\n(timings, severity = impact)
UN -> UN : RAISE ChatHealthyException  (on_missing_required = raise)

note over TOOL, CLIENT #f3f4f6
  A satellite's answer returns only as the internal callback. Every throw ends in
  the navigator — a middle tool re-raises, never swallows. The navigator is the
  one merge point: it sequences callbacks serially and its gate writes the one
  stream to the person.
end note
@enduml
